{
  "contract": "ADR-0021 §3 egress entry syntax and matching, v1",
  "keep_in_sync": "Source of truth: genfleet/sdk tests/fixtures/egress-hosts.cases.json. Copied byte-identical into genfleet/backend (DTO validator fixture). Change the SDK first, then re-copy.",
  "notes": [
    "entries: parse(input) is valid iff `valid`; `canonical` is the normalised form (port omitted when 443); `reason` is why an invalid entry is refused: invalid_host or ip_not_allowed.",
    "review_warning: true for every valid wildcard entry. There is no public-suffix list: `*.github.io` and `*.co.uk` are syntactically valid, and marketplace review decides; the admin review screen highlights entries with a warning. `*.com` is refused by the two-label rule, not by a suffix list.",
    "A host needs at least two labels; a wildcard `*.` needs at least two labels after it, so `*.com` is refused. Labels are LDH (letters, digits, hyphen; no leading or trailing hyphen), 1-63 chars; the host is at most 253 chars. Non-ASCII must be written as punycode.",
    "IP literals, including forms a resolver or a WHATWG URL parser reads as IPv4, are ip_not_allowed: a last label that is all digits or `0x` followed by zero or more hex digits (`127.1`, `2130706433`, `10.0.0x1`, `1.2.3.0x`, `10.0.0.0X`), more than one `:` (bare IPv6), or a leading `[`.",
    "Normalisation: ASCII whitespace trimmed from both ends, lowercase, one trailing dot dropped.",
    "limits: a list may hold at most `max_entries` entries; a longer one is refused with reason `limit`.",
    "matches: an exact pattern matches that host only; `*.x.y` matches any subdomain of x.y at any depth, never x.y itself. The port must be equal.",
    "A port is written without leading zeros: `:0443` is refused rather than read as 443, because parsers disagree on it (decimal vs octal).",
    "Order of checks, identical on every side: (1) refuse any character outside TAB, LF, VT, FF, CR and 0x20-0x7E (so U+FEFF, U+0085, U+00A0 and U+212A are refused, never trimmed or folded); (2) strip only ASCII whitespace (space, TAB, LF, VT, FF, CR) from both ends; (3) refuse anything left outside 0x21-0x7E, so internal whitespace and newlines are refused (an entry reaches a line-oriented proxy protocol); (4) lowercase. Patterns match the whole string."
  ],
  "limits": {
    "max_entries": 100,
    "max_host_length": 253
  },
